WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:03.503
I'd like to begin today by updating you
on our efforts to recover the debris

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.506
of several objects
that the United States Air Force shot down

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.709
over the last few days,
as well as that of the spy

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.012
balloon belonging to the People's
Republic of China.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:15.582
And I'd like to put into some context
for you

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.451
how we have worked and are still working

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:22.389
to better understand the issue of high
altitude, low speed craft.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.359
And let me start with the Chinese program.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.661
When President Biden came into office,
he directed the U.S.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:31.064
intelligence community
to do a broad assessment

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:34.801
of Chinese intelligence capabilities
and assure and to ensure

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.671
that we were working to detect
and to protect against them

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.440
I think for reasons

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.110
that you will all understand,
we cannot publicly go into many details

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.848
about how we discover and counteract
foreign intelligence collection.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:53.520
Efforts, because much of what we have done
and are doing is, of course, sensitive.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:59.192
But we were able to determine that
China has a high altitude balloon program

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:03.296
for intelligence collection that's
connected to the People's Liberation Army.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.498
It was operating

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:10.036
during the previous administration,
but they did not detected we detected it.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.038
We tracked it.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.041
And we have been carefully studying it
to learn as much as we can.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:19.412
We know that these PRC surveillance
balloons have crossed over

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.749
dozens of countries on multiple continents
around the world,

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:26.019
including some of our closest
allies and partners.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.055
We assessed that at this time.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:34.294
These balloons have provided limited
additive capabilities to the PRC's.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:38.331
Other intelligence
platforms used over the United States.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.336
But in the future, if the PRC continues
to advance this technology,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.006
it certainly could become more valuable
to them.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:50.243
The president also instructed
the intelligence community to take a broad

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:53.880
look at the phenomenon
of unidentified aerial objects.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:58.318
Indeed, President Biden conducted
the first ever daily intelligence briefing

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:02.288
session devoted to this phenomenon
back in June of 2021.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:06.359
He was briefed that this is not
just an issue for the United States

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.361
but one for the rest of the world.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:11.631
And as I said, our friends and our
partners are dealing with this as well.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:13.399
We worked

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.469
on a bipartisan basis
to stand up in office at the Pentagon

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.973
to study this in partnership
with the intelligence community,

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.009
academic institutions
and the private sector.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.981
These unidentified aerial phenomena
have been reported for many years

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.518
without explanation
or deep examination by the government.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.454
President Biden has changed all that.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:37.790
We are finally trying to understand them
better

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.627
now in light of the Chinese
balloon program

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.829
and this recent incursion
into our airspace.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.200
The United States and Canada
through North End have been more closely

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.205
scrutinizing that airspace, including
enhancing our radar capabilities, which,

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:57.277
as the commander of NORTHCOM and Noora
General Van Herc said just last night, may

00:02:57.277 --> 00:03:02.015
at least partially explain the increase
in the objects that have been detected.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:06.619
Slow moving objects at high altitude
with a small radar

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.522
cross-section
are difficult to detect on radar.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:13.092
Even objects
the size of the Chinese spy balloon

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:16.262
which had a payload
the size of roughly three school busses,

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:20.200
were not picked up by previous
administrations or other countries.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:21.968
We also know

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.003
that a range of entities
including countries,

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.738
companies, research and academic

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:29.576
organizations operate objects
at these altitudes for purposes

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:34.214
that are not nefarious at all,
including scientific research that said,

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.984
because we have not yet
been able to definitively assess

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:42.589
what these most recent objects are,
we acted out of an abundance of caution

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:47.060
to protect the security, our security,
our interest and flight safety

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.896
in Saturday's case.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.799
We acted in consultation
with the Canadian government.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:56.236
The president speaking personally
with Prime Minister Trudeau.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:04:01.307
The spy balloon was, of course, different
because we knew precisely where that was.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.909
As we have said,

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.612
we do not assess that
these most recent objects

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.114
posed any direct threat
to people on the ground,

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:11.451
and we are laser focused
on confirming their nature and purpose,

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:15.588
including through intensive efforts
to collect debris in the remote locations

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.422
where they have fallen.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.992
In each instance,

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:22.262
we have followed the same basic course.

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:27.300
We assessed whether they posed any kinetic
threat to people on the ground.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.235
They did not.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:32.205
We assessed whether they were sending
any communications signals.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.241
We detected none. We looked to see

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:38.311
whether they were maneuvering
or had any propulsion capabilities.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.080
We saw no signs of that.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.383
And we made sure to determine
whether or not they were manned.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.318
They were not.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:48.454
We did, however, assess
that their altitudes

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.457
were considerably lower
than the Chinese high altitude balloon

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:54.527
and did pose a threat
to civilian commercial air traffic.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.364
And while we have no specific reason
to suspect that they were

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:01.367
conducting surveillance of any kind,
we couldn't rule that out.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.637
That is why the president,
at the recommendation

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:08.308
of the secretary of defense,
the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:12.679
and the North NORTHCOM, nor any commander
gave the order to shoot them down.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:14.681
These missions

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:17.383
were completed successfully and safely.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.286
Efforts are actively underway right now
at all.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:23.022
Sites to find
what is left of those objects

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.692
so that we can better understand
and communicate with the American people

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.393
what they are.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.863
I think it's important
to remind the objects in Alaska

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.433
and Canada are in pretty remote terrain,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.536
ice and wilderness.

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:39.672
All of that making it difficult
to find them in winter weather.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.976
The object over Lake Huron now lies

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.512
in what is probably very deep water.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:50.950
So outside of recovery operations,
what are we doing?

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:54.354
Well, first, we are continuing to monitor.

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:58.257
There are no active tracks today.

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:01.194
But the professionals at North
will continue to do their important work.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.797
Secondly,
we are consulting with allies and partners

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:07.834
on the challenge
of identified aerial phenomenon

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.871
and how we can all work together
to deal with that challenge.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.308
The president
has directed the secretary of state,

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:17.543
secretary of defense,

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.679
and the director of National Intelligence
to engage

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.314
with their relevant counterparts,

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:24.550
to share information and to try to gain
their perspectives as well.

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:27.353
Again, this is an issue that affects
everybody around the world.

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:31.491
Third, we will continue to brief members
of Congress and relevant

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:34.727
state leadership on what we are doing
and what we learn.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:38.164
President has made this
a very top priority

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:42.001
We have over the course
of just the last few days and certainly

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:43.836
over the course of last week,

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:47.140
reached out to inform and brief members
of Congress and relevant state governors

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:50.443
of the operations that we were conducting
and the recovery operations

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:51.911
that are underway.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:56.382
We've also kept Congress briefed generally
on this issue of Chinese surveillance

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:59.819
balloons, including classified briefings
last August.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.956
And last week, administration officials
provided classified briefings

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:07.894
for all senators and all members of
the House of Representatives on the PRC.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.362
Surveillance balloon.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:12.031
We fully expect and anticipate and support

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.201
the ability to continue these
briefings in the days ahead.

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.470
And fourth,

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:18.137
the president,

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:22.208
through his national security adviser,
has today directed an interagency team

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:27.547
to study the broader policy implications
for detection, analysis and disposition

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.251
of unidentified aerial objects
that pose either safety or security risks.

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.720
Every element of the government

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.890
will redouble their efforts
to understand and mitigate these events.

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:40.860
And I'm happy to take some questions

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:42.662
John,

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:45.631
if the objects don't pose
a military threat

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:49.535
and they don't pose a threat
to the ground, why shoot them down?

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:52.438
Particularly because the military has

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:56.342
is routinely monitoring radar,
you know, radar blips.

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.912
I kind of cover that
in the opening statement.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:02.281
Two real reasons here First,

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:05.585
there was a very real potential risk
to civilian air traffic.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.120
The one shut down on Saturday.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.091
I'm sorry, yesterday was about 20,000 feet

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:16.462
and the two shut down Friday and Saturday.

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:17.997
We're at about 40,000 feet.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:21.300
And as you know, transcontinental air
traffic is roughly around 30,000 feet.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.402
It depends, of course, on weather.

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:26.405
And so because we assessed
that they weren't manned and weren't

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:30.510
being controlled and therefore left
to atmospheric conditions

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.515
the real risk to safety of flight
was, was a problem.

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:39.585
The second purpose and I talked about this
earlier too was even though

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:43.656
we had no indications
that any of these three

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.593
objects were surveilling,
we couldn't rule that out.

00:08:48.094 --> 00:08:51.597
And so there, you know, you want to err
on the side of safety here in terms of

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:54.600
protecting our national security interests
and the fact that these objects

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:58.938
could have and and likely did
at some point in their path,

00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:03.476
transit over you know, potential military
sites of ours or sensitive sites.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.013
So, again, out of an abundance of caution,
for those two reasons, the president,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.416
with the recommendation of his military
leaders, directed them

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:13.185
to be taken down
because it's so unprecedented.

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:16.956
Should the public be hearing
from the president directly on this?

00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:19.692
We have been

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:22.461
I think, as transparent as we can be.

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:25.565
I won't speak for the president's personal

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:31.003
speaking schedule, but,
I mean, he has been deeply engaged in

00:09:32.138 --> 00:09:33.606
every one of these decisions.

00:09:33.606 --> 00:09:37.143
He's been kept informed,
including as of this morning, on

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:42.114
what's going on with recovery efforts
And and he's very much

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:45.484
staying on top of the issue
and and directing his team

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:48.754
to make sure we are properly consulting

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:51.691
and briefing not just members of Congress,
but state leaders as well.

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:54.327
And, of course,
you know, we're also doing what we can

00:09:54.527 --> 00:09:57.797
in the public sphere in the early weeks
Sure.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:58.831
Excuse me.

00:10:00.266 --> 00:10:01.801
Thank you, John.

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:04.804
What is the president's
standard going to be going forward about

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:08.608
when he orders
an unidentified object shot down?

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.443
It comes down to

00:10:11.477 --> 00:10:14.347
one simple formulation, and that's

00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:16.849
if at the recommendation
of his military leaders,

00:10:16.849 --> 00:10:19.819
he believes that the safety
and security of the United States

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:21.554
the safety and security,
the American people,

00:10:21.554 --> 00:10:24.323
his prime responsibility warrant,
that kind of a decision.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.592
So it's possible
we could see these shutdowns

00:10:26.592 --> 00:10:28.594
on a regular basis
like we saw over the weekend.

00:10:28.628 --> 00:10:31.163
I don't think it's useful for me
to get ahead of where we are right now.

00:10:31.197 --> 00:10:32.498
The president will always side

00:10:32.498 --> 00:10:35.434
on preserving and protecting the safety
and security of the American people.

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:39.772
You've said we're not flying
any surveillance balloons over China.

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:43.042
Are we flying
any other kind of surveillance aircraft

00:10:43.042 --> 00:10:46.278
routinely over here now
flying surveillance balloons over China?

00:10:46.345 --> 00:10:49.382
I'm not aware of any other aircraft
that were flying over

00:10:49.915 --> 00:10:51.317
into India, Chinese airspace.

00:10:51.317 --> 00:10:55.588
And then finally, can you tell us
anything more about this octagonal object?

00:10:55.621 --> 00:10:58.858
How big was it?
We're still trying to assess

00:11:00.126 --> 00:11:01.560
what that was.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.663
I'm not going to get into a description.

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:06.432
I've seen the press reports about
what would it look like.

00:11:07.967 --> 00:11:09.669
I think we all need to be humble

00:11:09.669 --> 00:11:14.407
here in terms of what our ability
is to positively identify stuff

00:11:14.407 --> 00:11:18.244
from fighter aircraft that are going
several hundred miles an hour past

00:11:18.511 --> 00:11:22.081
essentially in terms of relative motion,
a stationary object

00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:25.217
that was not very big.

00:11:25.217 --> 00:11:28.654
So we don't know what this exactly looked
like.

00:11:28.654 --> 00:11:31.257
And again, we're still not sure exactly

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:34.560
what the purpose of it was
or who owned it.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.731
But we we hope to be able to find out more
once we can recover the debris

00:11:38.731 --> 00:11:42.068
from that one
and from the other two as well.

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:44.070
Just a few minutes ago, Prime
Minister Trudeau said

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:47.206
that there is some sort of pattern
to the objects over the last few days.

00:11:47.239 --> 00:11:48.841
Is that something you could elaborate on?

00:11:48.841 --> 00:11:50.810
What sort of pattern the White House see?

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.945
I'm not familiar
with the prime minister's comments,

00:11:52.945 --> 00:11:56.716
so I don't know if I
if I should take a swing at that.

00:11:56.716 --> 00:12:00.086
I would just tell you
that Going back to what I said before,

00:12:00.753 --> 00:12:03.556
these objects were not being maneuvered.

00:12:03.923 --> 00:12:06.392
They did not appear
to have any self propulsion.

00:12:07.193 --> 00:12:10.262
So the likely hypothesis is

00:12:10.262 --> 00:12:12.798
that they were being moved
by the prevailing winds.

00:12:13.532 --> 00:12:16.268
And maybe perhaps that's what
the prime minister's talking about.

00:12:16.268 --> 00:12:17.169
I don't want to speak for him.

00:12:17.169 --> 00:12:21.474
But certainly as the prevailing winds,
particularly at that altitude,

00:12:21.474 --> 00:12:26.178
go west to east or across the North
American airspace, I mean,

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:30.516
there was a general common movement
in that regard.

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:34.320
And you spoke at the top
kind of reassessing radar given

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.222
what happened with
with the initial balloon.

00:12:36.222 --> 00:12:38.491
Can you give us a sense? Can we expect?

00:12:38.991 --> 00:12:39.692
Should we assume

00:12:39.692 --> 00:12:41.961
that this is the regular number
of these objects

00:12:41.961 --> 00:12:43.729
over the United States,
that they've always been there

00:12:43.729 --> 00:12:46.031
and they just
haven't been looked at the same way

00:12:46.031 --> 00:12:49.935
or is there any reason to expect
that this is this is more than usual

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:52.538
that better flying?
So two thoughts here. I mean, I think

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:55.841
I think we can all

00:12:55.841 --> 00:12:58.611
get our heads around the fact that that

00:12:59.678 --> 00:13:01.881
there are sometimes

00:13:01.881 --> 00:13:04.917
things floating at high altitudes
for various purposes.

00:13:04.917 --> 00:13:07.853
As I said, scientific research, weather,

00:13:08.087 --> 00:13:10.289
weather, balloons, all manner of

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.859
of of innocuous craft

00:13:15.027 --> 00:13:17.463
can can be aloft at high altitudes.

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:20.900
I don't think that that's necessarily
unusual here.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:26.205
It's difficult for for me to say exactly
what you can expect going forward.

00:13:26.872 --> 00:13:29.341
One of the reasons that we think

00:13:29.742 --> 00:13:33.078
we're seeing more
is because we're looking for more.

00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:38.551
As you heard, the general van mentioned
last night, they have, um,

00:13:39.118 --> 00:13:42.521
they have modified the filters
in the gains, as we call it,

00:13:43.055 --> 00:13:45.291
of the, of the radar capabilities

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:48.160
to look more discreetly

00:13:48.661 --> 00:13:51.730
at high altitude, small radar

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:57.803
cross-section and low speed objects
And so if you do that and anybody

00:13:57.803 --> 00:14:01.140
that's operated radar will know
you can set you can set the parameters.

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:05.010
And if you set the parameters
in such a way that to look for a certain

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.947
something, it's more likely that
you're going to find a certain something.

00:14:08.547 --> 00:14:09.047
Okay.

00:14:09.315 --> 00:14:12.651
Given all you've discussed
are the actions the administration taking

00:14:12.651 --> 00:14:17.957
and what people have learned Chinese
by balloon this year in previous years,

